### Feature ResourceRoles — GUARDAR LA MATRIZ COMPLETA DE UN ROL (ISS-CR-02)
### Mismo endpoint que conceder (`POST /api/resource-roles`), pero con `resource_ids`:
###   { "role_id": 5, "resource_ids": [1, 2] }  -> 200 { message, result }
### Lo que no venga en la lista queda retirado (status = inactive).
### role_id 5 = AUDITOR_CLINICO (15 recursos, solo lectura).
### resource_id 1 y 2 = GET /api/patients y GET /api/patients/:id
###   (confírmalo antes en DBeaver: SELECT id, method, path FROM resources WHERE path LIKE '/api/patients%' ORDER BY id;)
### Al terminar, `npm run db:seed` deja la matriz de los 5 roles como estaba.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/session/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "admin",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

###

# @name loginAuditor
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/session/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "auditor",
  "password": "Auditor123!"
}

###

# @name loginFacturacion
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/session/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "facturacion",
  "password": "Facturacion123!"
}

@token = {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.access_token}}
@auditorToken = {{loginAuditor.response.body.$.access_token}}
@facturacionToken = 
@auditorRoleId = 5

### 1. ESTADO INICIAL — concesiones activas del auditor (15)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles?role_id={{auditorRoleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2. El auditor lee atenciones -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/encounters
Authorization: Bearer {{auditorToken}}

### 3. GUARDAR MATRIZ — el auditor queda solo con leer pacientes -> 200 (activated 0, deactivated 13, total_active 2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": {{auditorRoleId}},
  "resource_ids": [1, 2]
}

### 4. Persistencia — ahora solo 2 concesiones activas
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles?role_id={{auditorRoleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Efecto inmediato — atenciones ya no -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/encounters
Authorization: Bearer {{auditorToken}}

### 6. ...pero pacientes sí -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{auditorToken}}

### 7. Repetir el mismo guardado -> 200 con activated 0 y deactivated 0 (idempotente)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": {{auditorRoleId}},
  "resource_ids": [1, 2]
}

### 8. 400 — ID duplicado
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": {{auditorRoleId}},
  "resource_ids": [1, 1]
}

### 9. 400 — un recurso que no existe mezclado con uno válido (el 3 tampoco se concede)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": {{auditorRoleId}},
  "resource_ids": [1, 2, 3, 99999]
}

### 10. Sin cambios parciales — siguen siendo 2 concesiones (sin POST /api/patients)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles?role_id={{auditorRoleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. 400 — role_id como texto
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": "5",
  "resource_ids": [1]
}

### 12. 400 — resource_id y resource_ids a la vez (forma ambigua)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": {{auditorRoleId}},
  "resource_id": 1,
  "resource_ids": [1]
}

### 13. 404 — rol inexistente
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": 999,
  "resource_ids": [1]
}

### 14. 409 — ADMIN no se edita desde la matriz
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": 1,
  "resource_ids": [1]
}

### 15. 401 — sin token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": {{auditorRoleId}},
  "resource_ids": [1, 2]
}

### 16. 403 — con token, pero FACTURACION no tiene POST /api/resource-roles
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles
Authorization: Bearer {{facturacionToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": {{auditorRoleId}},
  "resource_ids": [1, 2]
}

### 17. Lista vacía — deliberado: el rol queda sin permisos (deactivated 2, total_active 0)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": {{auditorRoleId}},
  "resource_ids": []
}

### 18. El auditor ya no lee ni pacientes -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{auditorToken}}

### 19. La concesión individual sigue funcionando igual -> 201 (reactiva GET /api/patients)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": {{auditorRoleId}},
  "resource_id": 1
}

### RESTAURAR — en la terminal del backend: `npm run db:seed`
### (reconcilia los 5 roles: el auditor vuelve a sus 15 recursos)
